Short:        Use mpega.library under PPC (PUP/GCC)
Author:       cisc@c2i.net (Sigbjørn Skjæret)
Uploader:     cisc c2i net (Sigbjørn Skjæret)
Type:         dev/c
Replaces:     dev/c/MPEGAPPCdev.lha
Requires:     util/libs/mpega_library.lha
Architecture: ppc-powerup

Ooops, a small mistake made sure GCC would crash violently earlier .. fixed.

Fixed structure alignment issues so that everything works smoothly with GCC. ;)

Here's my current effort to get mpega.library working under PPC (PowerUP
(Sorry, I don't have a devkit for WarpOS, and don't know how to do this there))

I've now also added ppcinlines (untested, please report back) so it should work
with GCC and other compilers that need this special way of inlining functions.

Enjoy! ;)


